import Spaces.Supported.Inputs
import Spaces.Stacks.Bridges

/-!
# `D_{qc,Z}(X)` is compactly generated by a perfect complex (GL26 Lemma A.9, first half)

Guisado Villalgordo–Lank, *Relative Fourier–Mukai theory for algebraic spaces* (GL26),
**Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), over an algebraic space; the input
`SupportedCategoryInput.neeman_3_2_iii` of the scheme layer (`results/OPEN_INPUTS.md`,
row 2.10) is Neeman 2024, Theorem 3.2(iii).  For a quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic
space `X` and a closed `Z ⊆ |X|` with quasi-compact complement, this file proves, for the
category `D_{qc,Z}(X)`:

* `hasCoproducts`: `D_{qc,Z}(X)` has small direct sums (Stacks 08F3 and the remark preceding
  0AED);
* `lemma_A_9_generator`: it has a single compact generator `P`, a perfect complex supported
  on `Z` (Stacks 0AEC, 0AED): `P` is compact and every object receiving only zero maps from
  the shifts of `P` is zero (`IsPaperGenerator`, GL26 §2.1 / LP26 §2.1.2);
* `lemma_A_9_isCompactObject_iff`: its compact objects are exactly the perfect complexes
  supported on `Z` (Stacks 0AED);
* `lemma_A_9_triangEnvelope`: the compact objects are the thick (triangulated) envelope of
  `P` (Stacks 0GFD, the classical-generator half of Stacks 09SR);
* `lemma_A_9`: all of these together.

Non-vacuity: `nonVacuity_affine_univ` (an affine `X`, `Z = |X|`), `nonVacuity_base` (the
base `S` itself, `S` affine, e.g. `S = Spec ℤ` by `isAffine_terminal`); the instance arguments
come from `isTriangulated_qcohDerived` (06UQ) and `isTriangulated_support`.

## What is *not* proved: the preferred equivalence class

The last clause of the task (Neeman's Theorem 3.2(iii): the standard `t`-structure of
`D_{qc,Z}(X)` lies in the preferred equivalence class, `NeemanPreferredM6.InPreferredClass`)
is **not** proved here, for two reasons:

1. *Universe.*  `D(𝒪_X)` is AxiomMath's derived category at `HasDerivedCategory.standard`,
   with morphisms in `Type (u + 1)` and direct sums only indexed by `Type u` (a
   `Type (u + 1)`-indexed direct sum of `𝒪_X`-modules does not exist; AxiomMath,
   `StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean`).  The repository's
   `InPreferredClass`, `IsCompactAb` and `Coprod` use direct sums indexed by the morphism
   universe, here `Type (u + 1)`; the paper's compactness is `IsCompactObject.{u}` (direct sums
   indexed by `Type u`, the sets of the model).  A faithful rendering of the preferred class
   needs a small-Hom model of `D_{qc,Z}(X)` (AxiomMath's
   `Pretriangulated.exists_triangulatedEquivalence_of_locallySmall`) or a version of
   `InPreferredClass` with a separate coproduct universe.
2. *Mathematics.*  The preferred class needs, beyond 0AEC/0AED/09M8/09SR, a uniform bound
   `D^{≤ -A}_{qc,Z} ⊆ ⟨P⟩^{(-∞,0]}`.  The affine proof
   (`NeemanPreferredM6.inPreferredClass_of_compactlyGenerated`) uses the *equality* of the
   standard aisle with `Coprod (shiftTail P 0)` for the generator `A`, which is not available
   for a general qcqs `X`; there the inclusion is the content of Neeman's proof (an induction
   over a cover, in the spirit of Stacks 08GP), which AxiomMath does not contain.

## Rendering

* `D_{qc,Z}(X)` is the category `DqcZ X Z`, AxiomMath's `D_{QCoh,Z}(𝒪_X)`: the full
  subcategory of `D_qc(X)` on the objects whose cohomology sheaves are supported on `Z`.  Its
  image in `D(X)` is exactly the repository's `Spaces.DqcSupported X Z`
  (`dqcSupported_iff_exists`).  The category is AxiomMath's rather than
  `(DqcSupported X Z).FullSubcategory` because AxiomMath's theorems are stated for it.
* "Small direct sums" and "compact" are for direct sums indexed by `Type u`
  (`HasCoproducts.{u}`, `IsCompactObject.{u}`, Stacks 07LS).  Generation is zero detection by
  shifts (`IsPaperGenerator`, GL26 §2.1 / LP26 §2.1.2).
* "Perfect" is AxiomMath's `RingedSite.IsPerfect` on the small étale ringed site, which is
  the repository's `Spaces.Perf X` (Stacks 08G5) by definition (`perf_iff`).
* `D_{qc,Z}(X)` is pretriangulated through two `Prop` instances, `(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated`
  (Stacks 06UQ, `Spaces.Tag06UQInput`, proved in `SpacesVerified`) and
  `(CohomologySupportedOn … Z).IsTriangulated` (`SupportTriangulatedInput`); the statements
  take them as instance arguments, which `isTriangulated_qcohDerived` and
  `isTriangulated_support` produce from the inputs.
* `hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})` is the proof, on which absolute quasi-separatedness
  depends, that the site contains `Spec ℤ`; it always holds (`ContainsTerminalInput`).
* The file works in AxiomMath's instance context (see `Spaces/Supported/Inputs.lean`), in
  which AxiomMath's `QuasicoherentDerivedCategory` carries the triangulated structure.

## Assumptions

The tagged AxiomMath inputs of `Spaces/Supported/Inputs.lean` (08F3, 0AEC, 0AED, 0GFD, the
direct-sum and triangulated remarks preceding 0AED, and, for non-vacuity only, 03JX and
`BigFppfSite.contains_terminal`) and `Spaces.Tag06UQInput`; all are AxiomMath theorems, to be
discharged by the orchestrator in `SpacesVerified` (06UQ already is).  No other assumption:
in particular Neeman 2024, Theorem 3.2 is not used.
-/

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.Space RelativeWeakApprox

namespace RelativeFM.Spaces.Supported

universe u

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
  Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesGrothendieck

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard smallEtaleRingedSite_hasSheafify
  smallEtaleRingedSite_wEqualsLocallyBijective

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-! ### The category `D_{qc,Z}(X)` -/

/-- **`D_{qc,T}(X)`** (GL26 §2.2, `sec:prelim_stacks_perfects`) as a category: AxiomMath's
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)`, the full subcategory of `D_qc(X)` on the objects whose cohomology sheaves
are supported on `T`. -/
abbrev DqcZ (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) : Type (u + 1) :=
  (qcSupportedOn X T).FullSubcategory

/-- The inclusion `D_{qc,T}(X) ⥤ D(X)` (AxiomMath's `quasicoherentDerivedSupportedOnι`). -/
abbrev ιZ (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) :
    DqcZ X T ⥤ DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) :=
  (qcSupportedOn X T).ι ⋙ ObjectProperty.ι _

/-- The inclusion `D_{qc,T}(X) ⥤ D(X)` is fully faithful. -/
def fullyFaithfulιZ (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) :
    (ιZ X T).FullyFaithful :=
  (qcSupportedOn X T).fullyFaithfulι.comp (ObjectProperty.fullyFaithfulι _)

instance (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) : (ιZ X T).Full :=
  (fullyFaithfulιZ X T).full

instance (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) : (ιZ X T).Faithful :=
  (fullyFaithfulιZ X T).faithful

/-- The objects of `D_{qc,T}(X)` are exactly the objects of the repository's
`Spaces.DqcSupported X T`: an object `E` of `D(X)` lies in `DqcSupported X T` iff it is the
underlying object of an object of `D_{qc,T}(X)`. -/
theorem dqcSupported_iff_exists (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    (E : DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)) :
    DqcSupported X T E ↔ ∃ F : DqcZ X T, (ιZ X T).obj F = E :=
  ⟨fun hE => ⟨⟨⟨E, hE.1⟩, hE.2⟩, rfl⟩, by rintro ⟨F, rfl⟩; exact ⟨F.obj.property, F.property⟩⟩

/-- "Perfect" in `lemma_A_9` is the repository's `Spaces.Perf X`. -/
theorem perf_iff (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (E : DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)) :
    Perf X E ↔ (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect E :=
  Iff.rfl

/-! ### Triangulated structure -/

/-- `D_qc(X)` is a triangulated subcategory (Stacks 06UQ, `Spaces.Tag06UQInput`), in the
spelling of the instance arguments of this file. -/
theorem isTriangulated_qcohDerived (h : Tag06UQInput B S hS) (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) :
    (qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated :=
  h X.1 X.2

/-- `D_T(X)` is a triangulated subcategory (`SupportTriangulatedInput`). -/
theorem isTriangulated_support (h : SupportTriangulatedInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) :
    ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T) :=
  h X T

/-! ### Direct sums -/

/-- **Direct sums in `D_{qc,Z}(X)`** (Stacks 08F3 and the remark preceding 0AED): for `T`
closed, `D_{qc,T}(X)` has direct sums indexed by `Type u`, computed in `D_qc(X)`. -/
theorem hasCoproducts (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) (hT : IsClosed T) :
    HasCoproducts.{u} (DqcZ X T) := by
  have := h08F3 X.1 X.2
  intro J
  have := hsum X T hT J
  infer_instance

/-! ### Generation -/

/-- Zero detection in `D_{qc,T}(X)` by a family of maps in `D(X)`: if every object `E` of
`D_qc(X)` supported on `T` receiving only zero maps from the shifts of `P` (maps in `D(X)`) is
zero, then `P` is a generator of `D_{qc,T}(X)` in the sense of `IsPaperGenerator`. -/
theorem isPaperGenerator_of_detects (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated] (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)] (P : DqcZ X T)
    (hdet : ∀ E : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2,
      CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T E.obj →
        (∀ (n : ℤ) (g : P.obj.obj⟦n⟧ ⟶ E.obj), g = 0) → IsZero E.obj) :
    IsPaperGenerator P := by
  intro E hE
  let F := ιZ X T
  have hF := fullyFaithfulιZ X T
  refine IsZero.of_full_of_faithful_of_isZero F E (hdet E.obj E.property fun n g => ?_)
  have h := hE n (hF.preimage ((F.commShiftIso n).hom.app P ≫ g))
  have h' := congrArg F.map h
  rw [hF.map_preimage, Functor.map_zero] at h'
  rw [← cancel_epi ((F.commShiftIso n).hom.app P), h', comp_zero]

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), generator: for `X` quasi-compact
quasi-separated and `T ⊆ |X|` closed with quasi-compact complement, `D_{qc,T}(X)` has a
single compact generator `P` which is a perfect complex supported on `T`: `P` is perfect,
compact in `D_{qc,T}(X)` (`IsCompactObject.{u}`) and every object of `D_{qc,T}(X)` receiving
only zero maps from the shifts of `P` is zero (`IsPaperGenerator`).  From Stacks 0AEC and 0AED.
The preferred-class clause of Lemma A.9 is not part of this statement (module docstring). -/
theorem lemma_A_9_generator (h0AEC : Tag0AECInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]
    (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    ∃ P : DqcZ X T, (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect ((ιZ X T).obj P) ∧
      IsCompactObject.{u} P ∧ IsPaperGenerator P := by
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hPq, hPs, hdet⟩ := h0AEC hZ X hXqc hXqs T hT hTc
  let P' : DqcZ X T := ⟨⟨P, hPq⟩, hPs⟩
  exact ⟨P', hP, (h0AED hZ X hXqc hXqs T hT hTc P').2 hP,
    isPaperGenerator_of_detects X T P' fun E hEs => (hdet E hEs).2⟩

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), compact objects: for `X` quasi-compact
quasi-separated and `T ⊆ |X|` closed with quasi-compact complement, an object of
`D_{qc,T}(X)` is compact (`IsCompactObject.{u}`) iff it is a perfect complex.  Stacks 0AED. -/
theorem lemma_A_9_isCompactObject_iff (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ)
    (E : DqcZ X T) :
    IsCompactObject.{u} E ↔ (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect ((ιZ X T).obj E) :=
  h0AED hZ X hXqc hXqs T hT hTc E

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), compact objects, in the repository's
spelling: an object `E ∈ DqcSupported X T` is compact in `D_{qc,T}(X)` iff `E ∈ Perf X`. -/
theorem lemma_A_9_isCompactObject_iff_perf (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1)) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ)
    {E : DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)} (hE : DqcSupported X T E) :
    IsCompactObject.{u} (⟨⟨E, hE.1⟩, hE.2⟩ : DqcZ X T) ↔ Perf X E :=
  h0AED hZ X hXqc hXqs T hT hTc _

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), classical generation: for `X`
quasi-compact quasi-separated, `T ⊆ |X|` closed with quasi-compact complement, and `P` a
perfect generator of `D_{qc,T}(X)`, the compact objects of `D_{qc,T}(X)` are exactly the thick
(triangulated) envelope of `P`.  Stacks 0GFD with 0AED. -/
theorem lemma_A_9_triangEnvelope (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS) (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]
    (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ) (P : DqcZ X T)
    (hP : (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect ((ιZ X T).obj P))
    (hgen : IsPaperGenerator P) :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton P).triangEnvelope =
      IsCompactObject.{u, u + 1, u + 1} (C := DqcZ X T) := by
  let F := ιZ X T
  have hF := fullyFaithfulιZ X T
  have h := h0GFD hZ X hXqc hXqs T hT hTc P.obj.obj hP P.obj.property P.property
    fun E hEs hE => by
    let E' : DqcZ X T := ⟨E, hEs⟩
    have hz : IsZero E' := hgen fun n f => by
      apply F.map_injective
      rw [Functor.map_zero, ← cancel_epi ((F.commShiftIso n).inv.app P), comp_zero]
      exact hE n _
    exact F.map_isZero hz
  change (ObjectProperty.singleton P).triangEnvelope = _ at h
  rw [h]
  funext K
  exact propext (h0AED hZ X hXqc hXqs T hT hTc K).symm

/-- **GL26 Lemma A.9** (`lem:preferred_eq_class`), compact generation of `D_{qc,Z}(X)` over
an algebraic space.  Let `X` be a quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic space and `T ⊆ |X|`
closed with `|X| ∖ T` quasi-compact.  Then:

1. `D_{qc,T}(X)` has small (`Type u`-indexed) direct sums;
2. it has a single compact generator `P`, a perfect complex supported on `T`, whose thick
   envelope is the subcategory of compact objects;
3. its compact objects are exactly the perfect complexes (supported on `T`).

From Stacks 08F3, 0AEC, 0AED and 0GFD (AxiomMath).  **Difference from the paper**: the clause
"the standard `t`-structure of `D_{qc,T}(X)` lies in the preferred equivalence class"
(Neeman 2024, Theorem 3.2(iii)) is not included; see the module docstring for why it cannot
be stated with the repository's `InPreferredClass` in this model, and what it needs. -/
theorem lemma_A_9 (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h0AEC : Tag0AECInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS) (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS)
    (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) [(qcohDerived X).IsTriangulated]
    (hXqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (hXqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1)
    (T : Set (points B S hS X.1))
    [ObjectProperty.IsTriangulated (CohomologySupportedOn B S hS X.1 X.2 T)]
    (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : _root_.IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    HasCoproducts.{u} (DqcZ X T) ∧
      (∃ P : DqcZ X T, (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect ((ιZ X T).obj P) ∧
        IsCompactObject.{u} P ∧ IsPaperGenerator P ∧
        (ObjectProperty.singleton P).triangEnvelope =
          IsCompactObject.{u, u + 1, u + 1} (C := DqcZ X T)) ∧
      ∀ E : DqcZ X T, IsCompactObject.{u} E ↔
        (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect ((ιZ X T).obj E) := by
  refine ⟨hasCoproducts h08F3 hsum X T hT, ?_,
    lemma_A_9_isCompactObject_iff h0AED X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc⟩
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hPc, hPg⟩ := lemma_A_9_generator h0AEC h0AED X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc
  exact ⟨P, hP, hPc, hPg, lemma_A_9_triangEnvelope h0AED h0GFD X hXqc hZ hXqs T hT hTc P hP hPg⟩

/-! ### Non-vacuity -/

/-- The algebraic space represented by an object `T₀` of the big fppf site over `S`. -/
abbrev representedSpace (T₀ : BigFppfOver B S hS) : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
  ⟨yoneda.obj T₀, isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T₀⟩

/-- **Non-vacuity of the hypotheses of `lemma_A_9`**: an affine object `T₀` of the site
represents a quasi-compact (Stacks 03E3, `isQuasiCompact_yoneda_of_compact`) and quasi-separated
(Stacks 03JX, `AffineQuasiSeparatedInput`) algebraic space, and `Z = |X|` is closed with empty,
hence quasi-compact, complement.  For this choice `D_{qc,Z}(X) = D_qc(X)`. -/
theorem nonVacuity_affine_univ (hqs : AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u}))
    (T₀ : BigFppfOver B S hS) (hT₀ : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T₀)) :
    IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS (representedSpace T₀).1 ∧
      IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ (representedSpace T₀).1 ∧
      IsClosed (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS (representedSpace T₀).1)) ∧
      _root_.IsCompact (Set.univ : Set (points B S hS (representedSpace T₀).1))ᶜ := by
  refine ⟨isQuasiCompact_yoneda_of_compact B S hS T₀ inferInstance,
    hqs hZ T₀ hT₀, isClosed_univ, ?_⟩
  rw [Set.compl_univ]
  exact isCompact_empty

/-- Non-vacuity, a concrete affine object: over an affine base `S` (for instance
`S = Spec ℤ`, which every big fppf site contains, `ContainsTerminalInput`), the identity of
`S` is an affine object of the site, and it represents a quasi-compact quasi-separated
algebraic space; the hypothesis `hZ` of `lemma_A_9` is supplied by `ContainsTerminalInput`. -/
theorem nonVacuity_base [IsAffine S] (hqs : AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS)
    (hterm : ContainsTerminalInput.{u}) :
    IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS (representedSpace (Over.mk (𝟙 (B.obj hS)))).1 ∧
      IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS (hterm B)
        (representedSpace (Over.mk (𝟙 (B.obj hS)))).1 :=
  have h := nonVacuity_affine_univ hqs (hterm B) (Over.mk (𝟙 (B.obj hS))) ‹IsAffine S›
  ⟨h.1, h.2.1⟩

/-- Non-vacuity at the terminal base: `Spec ℤ` (the terminal scheme) is affine, so
`nonVacuity_base` applies to `S = ⊤_ Scheme` with `hS = hterm B`. -/
theorem isAffine_terminal : IsAffine (⊤_ Scheme.{u}) :=
  IsAffine.of_isIso (specULiftZIsTerminal.{u}.uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal).inv

/-- **Non-vacuity of `lemma_A_9` as a whole**: at an affine `X = h_{T₀}` with `Z = |X|`, every
hypothesis of `lemma_A_9` (including its two instance arguments, from 06UQ and
`SupportTriangulatedInput`) is met, and the lemma applies: `D_{qc,|X|}(X)` has small direct
sums and a compact perfect generator. -/
theorem lemma_A_9_affine_univ (h06 : Tag06UQInput B S hS)
    (hsupp : SupportTriangulatedInput B S hS)
    (h08F3 : Tag08F3Input B S hS) (hsum : SupportedDirectSumsInput B S hS)
    (h0AEC : Tag0AECInput B S hS) (h0AED : Tag0AEDInput B S hS) (h0GFD : Tag0GFDInput B S hS)
    (hqs : AffineQuasiSeparatedInput B S hS) (hterm : ContainsTerminalInput.{u})
    (T₀ : BigFppfOver B S hS) (hT₀ : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T₀)) :
    HasCoproducts.{u} (DqcZ (representedSpace T₀) Set.univ) ∧
      ∃ P : DqcZ (representedSpace T₀) Set.univ,
        (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS (representedSpace T₀).1 (representedSpace T₀).2).IsPerfect
          ((ιZ _ _).obj P) ∧ IsCompactObject.{u} P := by
  have := isTriangulated_qcohDerived h06 (representedSpace T₀)
  have := isTriangulated_support hsupp (representedSpace T₀) Set.univ
  obtain ⟨hqc, hqs', hcl, hco⟩ := nonVacuity_affine_univ hqs (hterm B) T₀ hT₀
  obtain ⟨hcop, ⟨P, hP, hPc, -, -⟩, -⟩ :=
    lemma_A_9 h08F3 hsum h0AEC h0AED h0GFD (representedSpace T₀) hqc (hterm B) hqs' Set.univ
      hcl hco
  exact ⟨hcop, P, hP, hPc⟩

end RelativeFM.Spaces.Supported
